# Auto-merge conflict avoidance for the branch -> main workflow
# (.github/workflows/auto-merge-claude.yml).
#
# Append-only logs are written by concurrent sessions that each add dated entries at the
# tail. When a session branch diverges from main, a plain `git merge --no-ff` conflicts in
# these files and the auto-merge job fails (exit 1), leaving the branch stranded and un-merged.
# The built-in `union` merge driver resolves such conflicts by keeping BOTH sides' added lines
# instead of emitting conflict markers -- correct behaviour for append-only logs.
#
# Do NOT add `merge=union` for in-place STATE files (Portfolio_Ledger.md, Regime_State.md,
# Watchlist.md, Strategy.md, Experiment_Parameters.md, the live Pending_*.md queues) or for
# full-overwrite cadence files (Daily.md, Weekly_*.md, Monthly_*.md, Quarterly_*.md): union
# would duplicate edited or whole-file content. Genuine concurrent edits to those are real
# conflicts that must be resolved, not unioned.

Decision_Log.md                  merge=union
Decision_Log_Archive_*.md        merge=union
Archived_Analysis.md             merge=union
Archived_Adversarial_Reviews.md  merge=union
